WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Module review · Financial Management
Recap: Financial Management

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Check that your first budgets, cash forecast, controls and reports tell one consistent story.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
You set up money management from the start: clear finance roles, organisational and project budgets, a funds register, a cash flow forecast, controls before the first payment, simple reports and financial health measures.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
One lesson at a time

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:38.881
9.1 Finance roles and the finance cycle: Bookkeeping records every transaction from the first payment; accounting reports by the rules; management finance helps you decide.

6
00:00:38.881 --> 00:00:48.259
9.2 The organisational budget: Your organisational budget plans the whole initiative, including founder pay and reserves, not just what funders cover.

7
00:00:48.259 --> 00:01:00.859
9.3 Project budgets, cost allocation and full cost recovery: A project budget includes direct costs and a fair share of the shared costs that make work possible.

8
00:01:01.259 --> 00:01:01.859
One lesson at a time

9
00:01:01.859 --> 00:01:11.237
9.4 Restricted and unrestricted funds: Restricted funds can only serve the funder’s purpose; unrestricted and designated funds remain your own decision.

10
00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:21.726
9.5 Cash flow, forecasting and runway: Cash, not a surplus on paper, pays the bills, and a monthly forecast shows gaps before they happen.

11
00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:32.844
9.6 Financial controls, approvals and procurement: Approvals, evidence, separation of duties and independent review are easiest to set up before the first payment.

12
00:01:33.244 --> 00:01:33.844
One lesson at a time

13
00:01:33.844 --> 00:01:42.852
9.7 Management accounts and budget versus actual: Simple, timely budget-versus-actual reports quickly show which of your first-year assumptions were wrong.

14
00:01:42.852 --> 00:01:52.600
9.8 Financial reporting: board, funders and statutory: Founders, funders, regulators and members each need different financial reports, some with fixed legal deadlines.

15
00:01:52.600 --> 00:02:04.089
9.9 Audit, examination and financial governance: Your form, size and country decide whether you need an independent examination or audit, so confirm thresholds early.

16
00:02:04.489 --> 00:02:05.089
One lesson at a time

17
00:02:05.089 --> 00:02:15.837
9.10 Financial health and sustainability: Financial sustainability is judged by financial health and resilience to shocks, not by how fast income grows.

18
00:02:16.437 --> 00:02:28.667
Your budgets, controls and reporting calendar feed the legal and risk work that follows, where financial duties, fraud and money risks get clear owners and responses.

19
00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:34.067
You check your Financial Management Pack and download each exercise as a PDF.

20
00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:38.667
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
